From 0d686360843c409ab26518c4a130e1ffc280da2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
Date: Mon, 29 Jun 2026 16:42:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] core/outputconfigurationstore: drop a runtime self-mirror
 in applyMirroring

An output can never mirror itself: kde_output_configuration_v2_apply() already
rejects a client config whose replicationSource is the output's own uuid ("%1
cannot mirror itself"). The json reader likewise refuses to load a stored
self-reference. But the same invalid state is reachable at runtime, with a
perfectly clean stored config, and nothing repairs it there.

Outputs that share an EDID are told apart only by connector name
(findOutputIndex() falls through to the name once the EDID identifier, EDID hash
and MST path all fail to disambiguate). DisplayLink docks expose exactly this:
two identical monitors, no MST path, and connectors that re-enumerate (rename,
and reappear one at a time) across a dock power-cycle. The connector-name -> uuid
binding is therefore unstable. At the same time a mirroring output keeps its
replicationSource in runtime state after its source output disappears -- there is
no cleanup, and applyQueuedChanges() preserves it via value_or(). When a connector
rename then re-matches that output to the stored identity whose uuid equals its
stale replicationSource, the output is mirroring itself.

This never reaches disk (the json reader drops it), so it cannot be cleared by
editing the stored config. It lives purely in the compositor's running state, and
because apply() rejects the whole configuration, kscreen -- which rebuilds every
config from the current, wedged state -- has every apply rejected in turn. All
outputs become unconfigurable until the session is restarted. It is easy to hit
with dual-head DisplayLink docks (identical EDIDs, connectors swap on
re-enumeration).

Enforce the invariant where every backend's generated configuration is assembled:
in applyMirroring(), if an output's resulting replicationSource equals its own
resulting uuid, clear it so the output falls back to a normal, non-mirrored
configuration. Set it explicitly to an empty string rather than leaving the change
unset, so a stale self-reference already on the output is actually overwritten
when the configuration is applied.

Signed-off-by: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
---
 src/outputconfigurationstore.cpp | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/outputconfigurationstore.cpp b/src/outputconfigurationstore.cpp
index 9322314c8b..4fcf241650 100644
--- a/src/outputconfigurationstore.cpp
+++ b/src/outputconfigurationstore.cpp
@@ -137,6 +137,21 @@ void OutputConfigurationStore::applyMirroring(OutputConfiguration &config, const
     }) | std::ranges::to<QList>();
     for (BackendOutput *output : enabledOutputs) {
         auto cfg = config.changeSet(output);
+        // An output can never mirror itself, but that invalid state is reachable at runtime even
+        // when the stored configuration is clean. Outputs that share an EDID (e.g. two identical
+        // monitors on a DisplayLink dock) are told apart only by connector name, which DisplayLink
+        // reshuffles across a dock power-cycle; combined with a replicationSource that is not
+        // cleared when its source output disappears, an output can end up re-matched to the very
+        // uuid its (stale) replicationSource points at. The json reader already drops such a
+        // self-reference on load; enforce the same invariant here, at the single point every
+        // backend's generated configuration passes through. Set it explicitly to an empty string
+        // rather than leaving it unset, so the stale value on the output is actually overwritten.
+        // Without this the self-mirror is committed and re-advertised, and every subsequent client
+        // configuration echoing it back is rejected ("cannot mirror itself"), leaving all outputs
+        // unconfigurable until the session is restarted.
+        if (cfg->replicationSource.value_or(output->replicationSource()) == cfg->uuid.value_or(output->uuid())) {
+            cfg->replicationSource = QString();
+        }
         const auto srcIt = std::ranges::find_if(enabledOutputs, [&cfg, &config, output](BackendOutput *other) {
             if (output == other) {
                 return false;
